  "description": "SEZGIR crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C58 H66 Gd4 N18 O20,0.25(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd1F (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd2F (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.962-4.136 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 105.55-120.14°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C58H66Gd4N18O20·0.25H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
